// Title: UAC Bypass Using EventVwr
// Sigma ID: 63e4f530-65dc-49cc-8f80-ccfa95c69d43
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Antonio Cocomazzi (idea), Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-04-27 | Modified: 2022-11-22
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, stealth
// Description: Detects the pattern of a UAC bypass using Windows Event Viewer
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/orange_8361/status/1518970259868626944?s=20&t=RFXqZjtA7tWM3HxqEH78Aw
//   - https://twitter.com/splinter_code/status/1519075134296006662?s=12&t=DLUXH86WtcmG_AZ5gY3C6g
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Eventvwr/#execute
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_uac_bypass_eventvwr.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\Microsoft\\Event Viewer\\RecentViews" or FolderPath endswith "\\Microsoft\\EventV~1\\RecentViews") and (not((InitiatingProcessFolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\System32\\" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\")))
